# Application Layer

Use cases (commands & queries) and DTOs — the "what" of the system.

Rules:
- Each use case is a class with methods for specific operations.
- Use cases depend ONLY on domain interfaces (repository ports) — never on
  concrete implementations or Django code.
- DTOs are plain data classes or DRF serializers that define the shape of
  data crossing the application boundary.
- Use cases NEVER import from `infrastructure/`.
- Use cases may import from `domain/` and from `core/`.

Files per bounded context:
- `use_case.py` — commands and queries
- `dto.py` — data transfer objects / serializers
